and alignment read off the ground file (a four-storey block about 110 by 40 m running along the quay at 122 degrees, the harbour basin to the north-east). No photographs were available and published descriptions are thin, so the building is modelled as a typical Frihavn warehouse of the 1940s: yellow brick, four storeys under a flat roof, a regular window grid, the loading doors on the quay side glazed, the foundation's galleries at the east end with a white-painted opened-up ground floor and an entrance canopy; the quay, bollards and harbour. Guessed: the brick colour, the windows, which end the galleries occupy, the neighbours."}